if (x !== y) return x < y ? -1 : 1;
```

The boundary comparison is likely incorrect: at exactly 30 days after payment, the function returns `false`, so the subscription remains active for one extra millisecond.

```js
function hasLapsed(lastPaidAt, now) {
  const THIRTY_DAYS = 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;
  return now.getTime() - lastPaidAt.getTime() >= THIRTY_DAYS;
